{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChUvKeMA1idQaxsD1E9df","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NokUPFUsG6bz1Eied3PsLJ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"mkdir -p .ard/468 && cat > .ard/468/plan.md <<'EOF'\n# Plan for #468\n\n## Implementation\n\nPolicy calls made here (a maintainer may overrule):\n- Commit-author emails seen in `git log` output DO count as PII and are replaced with `<email>`, except the allow-list below. A real person's address is still personal data in a log.\n- Allow-listed emails: `noreply@github.com`, `noreply@anthropic.com` (Co-Authored-By trailers) and anything ending `@users.noreply.github.com` (this covers the bot's own `<id>+<login>[bot]@users.noreply.github.com`). Reserved domains such as example.com or `.test` are NOT allow-listed, so a planted test address is redacted.\n- Allow-listed IPs: loopback (127.0.0.0/8, `::1`) and the unspecified addresses (`0.0.0.0`, `::`). Private ranges and documentation ranges are redacted.\n- Phones: only `+`-prefixed international numbers (7 to 15 digits, spaces, dots, dashes or parentheses allowed) and separated NANP forms (`(555) 123-4567`, `555-123-4567`, `555.123.4567`). Bare digit runs are never phones (timestamps, sizes, hashes).\n- Scanner logs that are flagged or fail redaction keep the raw log host-local, as issue-stage does, plus a marker file.\n\nPath audit (every place log or log-derived text reaches the repo or GitHub). Each must pass `Redactor.Text`/`Log` (secrets, paths, PII, scan):\n1. Committed logs, `closeout.prepareLog` (internal/closeout/prepare.go:460) and `Job.ExtraLogs` (prepare.go:~195-213): through `Redactor.Log`. Covered once `Log` gains the PII pass.\n2. Role file, `plan.md` and every other `.ard/<issue#>/` file: `red.Text` at prepare.go:157. Covered by the PII pass in `Text`.\n3. `cleanTail` (comment tail, prepare.go:489), `cleanReason` (prepare.go:534) and the reopened worker summary (prepare.go:~294): all use `red.Text`. Covered.\n4. Worker PR body, summary and fetched list: `job.setSummary` and `job.setFetched` (internal/worker/run.go:554-600), plus the PR body and code commit message builders in internal/worker (find with `grep -n \"Summary\\|Body\" internal/worker/*.go`). They use `Secrets.String` + `Scanner.Scan` directly and bypass `Redactor`. They need the PII pass added (see step 6).\n5. Scanner `issue.md` and the scanner status/streak notices: internal/scanner/pipeline.go after the guard (`CheckFindings`, internal/scanner/guard.go) near the @-mention defuse (~line 369). The guard only sees secrets. Add PII replacement on every finding field after the guard.\n6. Dry-run ledger `redactText` (internal/servecmd/serve.go:911): not committed; leave unchanged.\n7. Scanner local logs (`Handle.LogPath`, `Handle.StdoutPath`): step 4 below.\n8. Out of scope: worker code diffs (checked by the diff guard, not log-derived) and `serve.log`.\n\n### Steps\n1. New `internal/redact/pii.go`. Types: `type PIIOptions struct{ AllowEmails []string; AllowNets []netip.Prefix }`; `type PII struct{...}`; `func NewPII(o PIIOptions) (*PII, error)` (error on a bad allow entry; zero options give the defaults above); `func DefaultPII() *PII`; `func (p *PII) Bytes(b []byte) ([]byte, map[string]int, error)`; unexported `stream(ctx, r io.Reader, w io.Writer) (map[string]int, error)`. Work line by line with a `bufio.Reader`. A line over 1 MiB returns an error (fails closed). Placeholders are fixed: `<email>`, `<phone>`, `<ip>`; counts are keyed `pii:email`, `pii:phone` and `pii:ip`. Email: a hand-written ASCII local@domain matcher (regexp is fine), with the allow-list compared case-insensitively. IPv4: dotted quad with octets 0-255 and a boundary on both sides (previous and next byte not alphanumeric, and not `.` followed by a digit). IPv6: a candidate token of `[0-9A-Fa-f:.]` with at least two colons, validated with `netip.ParseAddr`. Phones as in the policy. Why: one pass, no new dependency, no placeholder can create a match.\n2. `internal/redact/redact.go`: add `PII *PII` to `Options` (nil means off). In `Log`, after `secrets.stream` flushes into the temp file and before the first scan, run the PII stream from that temp file into a second temp file in the same directory (0600), swap it in, and merge the counts into `Replaced`. Any error returns the existing zero-result error path and leaves no files. In `Text`, apply `PII.Bytes` after `secrets.Bytes` and before the scan; an error returns `fmt.Errorf(\"redact text: pii: %w\", err)`. Why: the scan sees the final text and both entry points get the pass.\n3. `internal/closeout/paths.go` `JobRedactor`: set `o.PII = redact.DefaultPII()` on both branches (builtin only, and Multi with gitleaks). The signature is unchanged. Update the doc comment. Why: the production redactor is the single place close-out gets its policy.\n4. Scanner local logs. New `internal/scanner/logredact.go`: `type LogRedactor interface{ Log(ctx context.Context, src, dst string) (redact.LogResult, error) }` and `func redactRunLogs(ctx, log *slog.Logger, mk func(executor.Handle) (LogRedactor, error), h executor.Handle)`. For each non-empty path in `h.LogPath` and `h.StdoutPath`: `Log(path, path+\".redacting\")`, then `os.Rename` onto the original only when `err == nil && !Flagged`. Otherwise remove the `.redacting` copy, leave the raw log, write a 0600 marker file `<path>.unredacted` (fixed text, no findings) and `log.Warn(\"scanner.log_unredacted\", \"job\", id, \"reason\", \"flagged\"|\"error\", \"rules\", ruleIDs)` with no finding text. A failure of `mk` is treated like an error. Add `NewLogRedactor func(executor.Handle) (LogRedactor, error)` to `ExecDeps` (internal/scanner/engine_exec.go:34). In `runJob` (engine_job.go) register a `defer` BEFORE the Cleanup defer, so it runs after Cleanup, once the process has stopped. It is a no-op when the field is nil (tests only). Check that nothing reads the scanner stdout after `finish` (AgentEngine.parse runs inside `finish`). Make the existing 7-day log sweep also remove `*.unredacted` markers (find it with `grep -rn \"7 \\* 24\\|logRetention\" internal/janitor internal/reaper`; the reaper deletes failed-job logs at internal/reaper/retention.go:65 and should drop the marker too).\n5. Wiring, internal/servecmd/scanners.go:28 where `scanner.ExecDeps` is built: set `NewLogRedactor` to wrap `closeout.JobRedactor(w.environ, w.hostPaths(), w.gitleaksOptions)` and call it with `closeout.Job{Worktree: h.Worktree, Home: h.Home}`. Why: the same environment secrets, host paths and gitleaks as issue-stage close-out.\n6. PII on the other paths. internal/worker: add `PII *redact.PII` to `Deps` (loop.go ~124, default `redact.DefaultPII()` in the defaults block at ~168), and apply it in `setSummary`, `setFetched` (treat a change as withheld, like secrets) and the PR body and commit-message builders found by the audit. internal/scanner/pipeline.go: add `PII *redact.PII` (nil means `DefaultPII()`) and apply it to title, body, files, group and fingerprint of each finding after the guard and before the defuse. Do not apply it to the fingerprint if that would break dedup: if the fingerprint changes, count that as a guard hit and file nothing.\n7. Commit-path test (`internal/closeout/commitpaths_test.go`, new). Parse internal/closeout/*.go (non-test) with go/parser. Assert that `stageFile(` is called only from an allow-list of functions (`prepareLog`, and the candidate staging in `Prepare`), and that every such function also calls `red.Log` or `red.Text`. Fail with a message pointing at this plan. Add the same kind of check in internal/worker for direct `Scanner.Scan` calls outside the allow-list, if it is simple; skip it if it is not.\n8. `docs/proposal.md`: in \"All agent output is committed too\" (line ~180) replace the \"Scanner run logs stay host-local in phase 0 ... not committed\" wording so it says scanner logs are redacted on disk at job end through the same redactor (secrets, host paths, PII, scan), keep only the redacted copy, and a flagged or failed log stays host-local with a marker and a log event. Keep \"committing scanner logs is a follow-up\". Add a PII paragraph: email, phone and IP, the placeholders, the allow-list, that git-log author emails count, and that the pass fails closed. In \"Committed output is redacted\" (line ~561) add the PII pass to the list, and say the worker PR body, commit message and scanner `issue.md` get it too. Run `make docs-check`.\n\n### Network inputs\nNone.\n\n### Test plan\nRun `make lint test`; add `go test -race ./internal/redact ./internal/closeout ./internal/scanner`. All tests are table-driven and offline.\n- internal/redact/pii_test.go, `TestPII`: email plain, email in a `git log` line (`Author: A B <a@corp.test>`), uppercase, an allow-listed `noreply@github.com`, `123+ard[bot]@users.noreply.github.com`, `x@users.noreply.github.com.evil.com` (must be redacted), two emails on a line, `@mention` and `user@` (no match); IPv4 `10.1.2.3` redacted, `127.0.0.1` and `0.0.0.0` kept, `999.1.1.1` and `v1.2.3.4` and `1.2.3.4.5` kept; IPv6 `2001:db8::1` redacted, `::1` kept, `12:34:56` kept; phones `+1 415 555 0100`, `(415) 555-0100`, `415-555-0100` redacted, `1700000000000`, `2026-11-28`, a sha256 and `1.2.3` kept. Expect the exact output text and counts.\n- Fail closed (`TestPIIFailsClosed`): a line over 1 MiB gives an error; `NewPII` with a bad allow entry gives an error; a cancelled ctx gives an error.\n- internal/redact/redact_test.go: `Log` and `Text` with PII on remove a planted token (known secret), email and IP together; PII nil leaves them (regression); a failing PII leaves no dst or temp file; a secret split across the PII placeholder cannot form a scan hit.\n- internal/closeout/paths_test.go: `JobRedactor` output has PII on (an issue-stage log holding token, email and IP commits as `[REDACTED:...]`, `<email>`, `<ip>`; `noreply` survives). Gitleaks off and on cases keep passing.\n- internal/closeout prepare tests: role file and `plan.md` containing an email commit with `<email>`; a broken redactor still commits nothing (existing `brokenRedactor`).\n- internal/closeout/commitpaths_test.go: passes now; add a negative table case on a synthetic source string to prove the checker fails on an unredacted `stageFile` call.\n- internal/scanner/logredact_test.go: a fake executor and agent that prints a planted token, email and IP into the log and stdout; after `runJob` neither file holds them and the file mode is 0600. A flagged log (an unknown-shape secret the builtin scan flags) keeps the raw log, writes the marker and logs no finding text. A redactor that errors does the same. A nil `NewLogRedactor` is a no-op. The redacted file replaces the original only on success, and no `.redacting` file is left.\n- internal/scanner pipeline test: a finding body with an email files `<email>` in `issue.md`.\n- internal/worker tests: summary with an email is redacted; PR body too.\n- Edge cases: an empty log, CRLF, a log with no trailing newline, a very long line (fail closed), UTF-8 and invalid bytes next to an email.\n\n### Risk\nMedium. The redactor is security-sensitive and used by every close-out, so a PII false positive can change committed text or block a commit (an error on a very long line). The allow-list and phone and IP rules are the tuning risk. The scanner hook touches the job runner but only after `finish`. No migration, no protected paths from merge.protected_paths (all changes are Go code and docs/proposal.md). `redact.Options` gains an optional field and `JobRedactor` keeps its signature. No concurrency change beyond the existing deferred cleanup order.\n\n### Size\nL. About 900 to 1,400 changed lines including tests. Files: internal/redact/pii.go (new), pii_test.go (new), redact.go, redact_test.go; internal/closeout/paths.go, paths_test.go, prepare_test.go, commitpaths_test.go (new); internal/scanner/logredact.go (new), logredact_test.go (new), engine_exec.go, engine_job.go, pipeline.go and its tests; internal/servecmd/scanners.go; internal/reaper/retention.go or the janitor sweep; internal/worker/loop.go, run.go and tests; docs/proposal.md.\nEOF\ncat > .ard/468/triage-engineer.md <<'EOF'\n---\nrole: engineer\nstatus: done\nattempt: 1\n---\nAdds a fail-closed PII pass (email, phone, IP with an allow-list) to the shared redactor, runs scanner job logs through the close-out redactor locally at job end, and covers the worker and scanner paths that bypass it. It also adds a commit-path test and the proposal edits. Size L, risk medium because every close-out uses the redactor.\n\n## Open issues\n- Policy call to confirm: commit-author emails in git log output are treated as PII and replaced, except noreply GitHub and Anthropic addresses.\n- A PII false positive (for example a version string shaped like an IP) can alter committed text. A line over 1 MiB fails closed and keeps the log host-local.\n- Flagged or failed scanner logs stay raw on the host with a marker file. The existing 7-day sweep must be extended to remove the marker.\nEOF"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3288,"cache_read_input_tokens":46476,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3288},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2cd02ebb-e986-4749-a632-93caae21dd5c","uuid":"64a21a37-5ed8-4775-adef-2c8489e031b0","timestamp":"2026-11-28T07:20:15.223Z","request_id":"req_011ChUvKeDTsndggrBLe8LrU"}
